### MapManager::Config ###
Each <Map> here configures one map. Maps not listed use engine defaults.
  Number           Map id (matches the map numbers used everywhere else,
                    e.g. MapServerInfo.xml's MapNumber).
  PK               -1 = use the server-wide default (GameServer.ini)
                     1 = force non-PK / safe zone on this map
                     0 = force PK enabled on this map
  Range             View range in tiles.
  ExpRate           Experience rate, percent (100 = normal, 200 = double).
  ItemDropRate      Item drop rate, percent (100 = normal, 200 = double).
  ExcItemDropRate   Excellent item drop chance, out of 1,000,000
                     (1000 = 0.1%, 10000 = 1%, 1000000 = 100% guaranteed;
                     values above 1000000 have no extra effect).
  SetItemDropRate   Set item drop chance, out of 1,000,000 (same scale
                     as ExcItemDropRate).
  SocketItemDrop     1 = socket items can drop on this map, 0 = cannot.
  Helper            1 = MU Helper (auto-pathing/bot assist) allowed here,
                     0 = disabled.
  Gens              1 = Gens (faction) battle rules apply here, 0 = don't.
  Attack            1 = the CustomAttack (auto-attack/farm) command is
                     allowed on this map, 0 = blocked.
  Store             1 = personal store (CustomStore, online and offline)
                     can be opened on this map, 0 = blocked.
  Pick              1 = the CustomPick (auto-pickup) command is allowed
                     on this map, 0 = blocked.
  Trade             1 = player-to-player trade requests are allowed on
                     this map, 0 = blocked.
  GuildWar          1 = guild war can be declared while the requester or
                     the target guild's master is on this map, 0 = blocked.
  AccountLevel      -1 = no restriction. N = minimum VIP AccountLevel
                     (0-3) required to enter this map, enforced both via
                     the "Move" NPC command and by walking onto any gate/
                     portal that leads here. Does not affect other ways
                     of reaching the map (events, GM commands, etc.).
  CashShop          1 = the Cash Shop can be opened while on this map,
                     0 = blocked.
  Summon            1 = the Dark Lord's "Summon" skill can pull party
                     members onto this map, 0 = blocked (they stay put
                     and get a notice instead).
  Resurrection      1 = the Resurrection Talisman can bring its owner
                     back to this map, 0 = blocked.
  Mobility          1 = the Mobility Talisman can bring its owner back
                     to this map, 0 = blocked.
  Name              Free-text label, for readability only (not read by
                    the loader).

STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

